description:
Design a 3-to-4 multiplexer where inputs a, b, and c control the output lines w, x, y, and z. The output w always reflects the value of a. The output x is driven by a when b is high, while it remains in a high-impedance state when b is low. Similarly, the output y is driven by a when the negation of b is high, also going to a high-impedance state when b is high. The output z directly represents the value of input c.
module top_module(
    input a, b, c,
    output w, x, y, z
);

code:
module top_module(
    input a, b, c,
    output w, x, y, z
);wire [1:0] sel;
assign sel = {b, ~b};

assign w = a;
assign x = sel[0] ? a : 1'bz;
assign y = sel[1] ? a : 1'bz;
assign z = c;

endmodule

