description:
Design a circuit that compares two N-bit wide input values, `a` and `b`, to determine if `a` is greater than `b`. This module computes the difference `b - a` and outputs a single bit `a_gt_b`, which is asserted (high) when `a` is less than or equal to `b`, as indicated by the sign bit of the difference. The default parameter N is set to 32, implying that the circuit is intended to handle 32-bit input values, but it can be adjusted for other bit-widths as needed.
module top_module(
    a,
    b,
    a_gt_b
);

code:
module top_module(
    a,
    b,
    a_gt_b
);parameter N = 32;

    input   [N-1:0] a;
    input   [N-1:0] b;
    output          a_gt_b;

    wire    [N-1:0] diff;
    assign diff = b - a;
    assign a_gt_b = diff[N-1];
endmodule

