description:
Design a circuit that detects the rising edge of a button press. The module captures the button state across multiple clock cycles, creating a delayed version of the button signal. The output, `outedge`, is high when the current button state is high (btn_d2) and the previous state was low (btn_d3), effectively indicating a transition from low to high (rising edge) of the button signal.
module top_module(  input clk, btn,
                    output outedge );

code:
module top_module(  input clk, btn,
                    output outedge );reg  btn_d1, btn_d2, btn_d3;


always @(posedge clk)
begin
    btn_d1 <= btn;
    btn_d2 <= btn_d1;
    btn_d3 <= btn_d2;
end


assign outedge = btn_d2 & ~btn_d3;

endmodule

