Design a UART receiver that captures incoming serial data. The module continuously monitors the `uart_rx` line for a start bit and, upon detecting it, samples the incoming bits at predetermined intervals using a baud rate clock. The state of the bit counter helps manage the timing of the sampling process, indicating when a full 8-bit character has been received. When the data is available, the `valid` output signal indicates readiness for reading, while the received data is presented on an 8-bit output bus. The system is reset upon a low signal on `resetq`, initializing the state variables and preparing for new data reception.
