Design a circuit that implements a one-bit full adder. The module takes three one-bit inputs: a, b, and c_in (the carry-in). It outputs a one-bit sum and a carry-out (c_out). The full adder uses two half adders to compute the sum and propagate the carry, where the first half adder computes the sum of inputs a and b, and the second half adder combines the result of the first half adder with c_in. The final carry-out is determined by an OR gate that combines the carry outputs from both half adders.
