description:
Design a sign-extension module that adjusts a 32-bit input offset into a 64-bit output based on specific criteria. The module examines the most significant bits of the offset to determine how to extend it: for an offset starting with the binary pattern `000101`, it utilizes the lower 26 bits for construction; for the pattern `10110100`, it takes the 20 bits from a different range; otherwise, it processes a smaller segment of 10 bits. The extended value is filled with sign bits to preserve the sign of the original value, thereby allowing for proper representation in a wider bit field for subsequent processing in a wider data path.
module top_module(
    offset,
    signExtend_offset
    );

code:
module top_module(
    offset,
    signExtend_offset
    );input [31:0] offset;
    output reg [63:0] signExtend_offset;

    always@(offset)
    begin

        if (offset[31:26] == 6'b000101) 
        begin
            signExtend_offset[25:0] = offset[25:0];
            signExtend_offset <= {{38{signExtend_offset[25]}}, signExtend_offset[25:0]};
        end
        else if (offset[31:24] == 8'b10110100)  
        begin
            signExtend_offset[19:0] = offset[23:5];
            signExtend_offset <= {{44{signExtend_offset[19]}}, signExtend_offset[19:0]};
        end
        else
        begin 
             signExtend_offset[9:0] = offset[20:12];
             signExtend_offset <= {{54{signExtend_offset[9]}}, signExtend_offset[9:0]};
        end
    end
endmodule

