description:
Develop a sequential circuit that captures and propagates a single-bit input signal through two stages of registers on the rising edge of the clock. The circuit takes an input `a` and, with each clock cycle, updates the output `q` to reflect the value of `a` as it progresses through the intermediate register `q1`, ultimately producing `q` as the delayed version of `a` by two clock cycles.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input a,
  output reg q
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input a,
  output reg q
);reg q1, q2;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  q1 <= a;
  q2 <= q1;
  q <= q2;
end

endmodule

