description:
Design a digital clock circuit that counts and displays time in hours, minutes, and seconds using 4-bit registers. The clock advances on each positive edge of the clock signal (Clk) and can be loaded with initial time values when the active-low load signal (nLoad) is asserted. The module increments the seconds continuously and rolls over to the next minute after 59 seconds, subsequently managing minute and hour overflow, ensuring proper time formatting and wrapping (e.g., 24-hour format).
module top_module(nLoad, Clk, hour2, hour1, minute2, minute1, second2, second1, 
						chour2, chour1, cminute2, cminute1, csecond2, csecond1);

