Design a single-port 8KB RAM module that functions with a read-first mode. It synchronously writes data when a write signal is active and the clock is at a positive edge, while asynchronously providing output data based on the specified address. The RAM is initialized to zero on reset and can store 32-bit data entries indexed by a 11-bit address. The module is intended for use in a data cache (icache) system where read and write operations are essential for managing stored values.
module top_module(
    // Inputs
     input           clk_i,
     input           rst_i,
     input  [ 10:0]  addr_i,
     input  [ 31:0]  data_i,
