description:
Design a frequency divider that reduces the input clock frequency by a specified divisor value. The module takes a clock input (clk_in) and a reset signal. Upon receiving a rising edge on clk_in or reset, it either initializes the output clock (clk_out) and internal counter or toggles clk_out every 'divisor' clock cycles, effectively generating an output clock signal at a lower frequency. The design is suitable for applications requiring clock signal modulation or timing adjustments.
module top_module(
  input clk_in,
  input reset,
  output reg clk_out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk_in,
  input reset,
  output reg clk_out
);parameter divisor = 2; // value by which to divide the input frequency

always @(posedge clk_in or posedge reset) begin
  if (reset) begin
    clk_out <= 0;
    counter <= 0;
  end else begin
    if (counter == divisor-1) begin
      clk_out <= ~clk_out;
      counter <= 0;
    end else begin
      counter <= counter + 1;
    end
  end
end

reg [31:0] counter = 0;
endmodule

