description:
Design a watchdog timer that monitors an input clock signal and resets an output signal after a specified timeout period. The module includes an 8-bit counter that increments on each clock pulse and triggers the watchdog output (wdt) to a high state once the counter reaches the defined timeout value of 100 clock cycles. Additionally, the counter can be reset by asserting the reset input (rst), which also brings the watchdog output back to low. This circuit is essential in applications where it is crucial to detect system hangs or malfunctions by ensuring the system is responsive within a given timeframe.
